  "hints": [
    "without parentheses, this is easy: keep a running result and a current sign, applying each number as you read it. what does '(' really do to that running process?",
    "when you hit '(', you need to pause your current result and sign, and start fresh for what's inside - what structure lets you resume exactly where you paused once ')' is reached?",
    "before entering '(', push your current result and the sign that will apply to the whole parenthesized group once it's done, then reset result to 0 and sign to positive",
    "on ')', pop the saved sign and previous result, and combine: newResult = poppedResult + poppedSign * currentResult; continue processing after the parenthesis with this combined value"
  ],
  "commonMistakes": [
    "forgetting to reset the running result to 0 when entering a new parenthesis level",
    "applying the sign before the parenthesis to only the first term inside it instead of the whole parenthesized result",
    "mishandling multi-digit numbers by not accumulating consecutive digit characters before applying the sign"
  ],
  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You're given a string representing a mathematical expression made up of non-negative integers, '+', '-', parentheses '(' ')', and spaces.\n\n**Evaluate the expression and return its integer result.**\n\nThere is no multiplication or division to worry about, only addition, subtraction, and nested parentheses that can change evaluation order.\n",
    "constraints": [
      "1 <= s.length <= 3 * 10^5",
      "s consists of digits, '+', '-', '(', ')', and ' '",
      "s represents a valid expression",
      "'-' may be used as a unary operator, e.g. \"-1\" or \"-(2 + 3)\"",
      "every number and running calculation fits in a signed 32-bit integer"
    ],
    "notes": [
      "a negative number right after an opening parenthesis, e.g. \"(-1+2)\"",
      "deeply nested parentheses",
      "an expression with no parentheses at all, just a chain of + and -"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "Arguments passed into solution function",
    "outputFormat": "Return output matching method signature",
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "s = \"1 + 1\"",
        "output": "2",
        "expectedOutput": "2",
        "explanation": ""
      },
      {
        "id": "sample_2",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "s = \" 2-1 + 2 \"",
        "output": "3",
        "expectedOutput": "3",
        "explanation": "spaces are ignored; evaluated left to right as (2-1)+2 = 3"
      },
      {
        "id": "sample_3",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "s = \"(1+(4+5+2)-3)+(6+8)\"",
        "output": "23",
        "expectedOutput": "23",
        "explanation": "inner parens evaluate first: (4+5+2)=11, so (1+11-3)=9, and (6+8)=14; 9+14=23"
      }
    ],
